/rust/target/

# Core dumps, e.g. from a crash under `go test -race`.
core
core.*

# Locally built native libraries.
#
# These ARE shipped -- they have to be in the tree, because a Go module zip is
# built from the repo at a tag. Only the build-libs workflow should commit
# them, after its smoke jobs have run the Go suite against each one on real
# hardware.
#
# This block only helps before the workflow has ever committed them: ignore
# rules do not apply to tracked files, so once they are in the index a `git
# add -A` after `make lib` picks them up again regardless. The enforcement is
# the no-hand-built-libs job in .github/workflows/ci.yml. See
# docs/RELEASING.md.
libs/*/lib/iroh_go.lib
libs/*/lib/iroh_go.lib.sha256
